    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Occupying a prominent corner site along the spectacular Wild Atlantic Way, approximately 7 kilometres west of Louisburgh, Co. Mayo, this exceptional mixed-use property presents a rare opportunity to acquire a spacious family residence together with substantial adjoining commercial accommodation, all enjoying an unrivalled coastal setting and exceptional future potential.\r\nCommanding panoramic views across Clew Bay towards Clare Island and Croagh Patrick, the property occupies a highly visible roadside position at the junction leading to the renowned P. Dan’s Bar & Restaurant and The Big Style Lodge. It also enjoys a strategic location on the main road to Silver Strand and White Strand beaches and serves as one of the principal access routes to Mweelrea Mountain, Connacht’s highest peak, making it an ideal location for those seeking to capitalise on the area’s thriving tourism and outdoor recreation.\r\nThe property is offered for sale as one complete holding, although consideration may also be given to selling the residential and commercial elements separately.\r\n\r\nResidential Bungalow\r\nThe well-appointed three-bedroom semi-detached bungalow offers bright, spacious and versatile accommodation and, with modest modernisation, would make an ideal family home, retirement residence, holiday home or investment property.\r\nThe accommodation briefly comprises:\r\n•\tEntrance Hall\r\n•\tSpacious Sitting Room\r\n•\tOpen Plan Kitchen / Dining / Living Area\r\n•\tConservatory\r\n•\tPantry / Utility Area\r\n•\tThree Bedrooms\r\n•\tTwo Ensuite Bathrooms\r\n•\tMain Family Bathroom\r\nThe residence, with an approximate internal floor area of c.134.08 sq.m (c.1,443.22 sq.ft) provides generous living accommodation in a spectacular coastal setting and offers an excellent opportunity to create a wonderful home in one of Mayo’s most scenic locations.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFormer Shop Premises\r\nAdjoining the residence is a substantial former retail premises extending to approximately c.85.44 sq.m (c.920 sq.ft).\r\nAlthough no longer trading, the building offers outstanding potential for a variety of future commercial or residential uses (subject to the necessary planning permissions), including:\r\n•\tConvenience Store\r\n•\tCafé or Artisan Food Business\r\n•\tCraft or Gallery Space\r\n•\tOffice Accommodation\r\n•\tTourism Enterprise\r\n•\tWorkshop or Studio\r\n•\tResidential Conversion (STPP)\r\nIts prominent roadside position and generous frontage make it ideally suited to a wide range of future opportunities.\r\n\r\nFormer Public House / Apartment\r\nTo the rear of the commercial premises is a substantial building extending to approximately c.137.95 sq.m (c.1,485 sq.ft), formerly operating as a public house before being converted during the 1980s into a spacious one-bedroom apartment.\r\nThe apartment has been vacant for some time and may qualify for available refurbishment and vacant property grant schemes, subject to eligibility.\r\nThe accommodation offers exciting potential for refurbishment or reconfiguration, including conversion into a spacious two-bedroom residence or holiday accommodation (subject to any necessary planning permission).\r\n\r\n\r\nOutside\r\nThe property enjoys a corner site with generous off-street parking and exceptional frontage.\r\nA former petrol forecourt remains to the front of the property, offering further potential, subject to the necessary statutory approvals.\r\nThe generous corner site, combined with its outstanding visibility and coastal setting, creates a property of exceptional versatility and long-term potential.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDevelopment Potential\r\nOne of the property’s greatest strengths is its flexibility.\r\nThe commercial buildings offer significant scope for refurbishment, redevelopment or alternative uses (subject to planning permission). Equally, purchasers may consider the site suitable for the construction of a replacement dwelling or other residential development, subject to obtaining the necessary planning consent.\r\nThe property is likely to appeal to:\r\n•\tFamilies\r\n•\tInvestors\r\n•\tDevelopers\r\n•\tTourism & Hospitality Operators\r\n•\tLifestyle Buyers\r\n•\tBusiness Owners seeking a Live/Work Opportunity"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "\tPrime corner site on the Wild Atlantic Way with coastal views towards Clare Island & Croagh Patrick\r\n\tThree-bedroom semi-detached bungalow - Two ensuite bathrooms plus family bathroom\r\n\tFormer retail premises extending to approximately c.1,000 sq.ft.\r\n\tFormer public house converted to a one-bed apartment extending to approximately c.1,000 sq.ft.\r\n\tPotential eligibility for refurbishment and vacant property grants (subject to qualification)\r\n\tExtensive gardens and generous roadside parking\r\n\tFormer petrol forecourt offering additional future potential\r\n\tExcellent frontage on the main road to Silver Strand and White Strand beaches\r\n\tSituated on the principal access route to Mweelrea Mountain\r\n\tSignificant redevelopment opportunities (subject to planning permission)\r\n\tSuitable for residential, commercial, tourism or mixed-use purposes\r\n\tOffered for sale as one lot"
      },
